}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,0)$, $(0,-3)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(12,-24)$\n- $(8,16)$\n- $(2,-4)$" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284110 1113 #uuid "88e719bc-e349-5ca0-a13c-a121f56b9351" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284110 1145 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -24 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-4)$, $(12,-24)$ and $(-8,16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284112 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284113 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284114 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284115 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284116 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1041 "selection" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284113 13194139534362 true] [17592186284111 1110 #uuid "be65ef3d-5052-5673-a3d9-6e70ca192993" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284112 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284112 1111 #uuid "f35c6757-c1cc-5e95-adc9-7f3b43987bee" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284113 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284113 1111 #uuid "f3aab5aa-276e-5326-bbfe-4b9e1ca11ad8" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284114 1034 "III only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284114 1111 #uuid "58ad1e6b-adf3-52cd-aecb-ac30e59feb28" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284115 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284115 1111 #uuid "cda1164d-4de5-56fe-ab02-1b31eb5243b7" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284116 1034 "II only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284116 1111 #uuid "73c06a27-23a8-5503-bac0-b74613d69742" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284117 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284118 13194139534362 true] [17592186284117 1089 "q-147671" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534362 true] [17592186284117 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-1),(0,2),$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(6,-1)$\n- $(7,-14)$\n- $(8,-16)$" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284117 1113 #uuid "6364a192-b48f-5703-8297-b5247d60439d" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284117 1145 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 12 & -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(8,-16),$ $(-6,12)$, and $(7,-14).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284119 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284120 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284121 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284122 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284123 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1041 "selection" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284119 13194139534362 true] [17592186284118 1110 #uuid "41075aa9-0276-571b-a372-d1c938d5d900" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284119 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284119 1111 #uuid "ee5af7d6-ac78-5d00-8c37-da4bcfdf7a70" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284120 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284120 1111 #uuid "820502db-e4d6-55f6-9fdc-553dfcad78b8" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284121 1034 "I only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284121 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284121 1111 #uuid "838c1b7a-be1e-5ec4-b336-551b12185475" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284122 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284122 1111 #uuid "5ee21e47-6f22-5717-8570-01e475c9354a" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284123 1034 "II only" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284123 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534362 true] [17592186284123 1111 #uuid "635d14e7-39d4-5aa7-b218-5ecef799c9bd" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284124 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284125 13194139534362 true] [17592186284124 1089 "q-162199" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284124 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534362 true] [17592186284124 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/eb1247ddcaaf12a342aa036550ed4f9f7daaeb6037e7ebbab0de619bb6975dbe.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the pentagon shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284124 1113 #uuid "1f5f7e14-de4a-5b80-a0ab-301a0dcb6346" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284124 1145 "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nSince $T$ is the zero matrix, the image of our object under the action of $T$ is the origin." 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284126 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284127 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284128 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284129 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284130 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1041 "selection" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284126 13194139534362 true] [17592186284125 1110 #uuid "7db89d2d-1270-5238-a5d8-8337010a987f" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284126 1034 "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" 13194139534362 true] [17592186284126 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 1319413